

RESOLV.CONF(5)      UNIX Programmer's Manual        RESOLV.CONF(5)



NAME
     resolv.conf - resolver configuration file

DESCRIPTION
     The file /etc/resolv.conf configures the FGX name resolver
     used by gethostbyname(3).  dhclient(8) rewrites the nameserver
     line from the DHCP lease at boot; a search domain may be added
     by hand.  Blank lines and lines beginning with `#' are
     ignored.  The recognized directives are:

     nameserver a.b.c.d
          The IP address of the DNS server to query.  Only the
          first nameserver line is used.

     search domain ...
          Domains appended to an unqualified name (one with no
          dot) before it is looked up: with `search example.com',
          the name `www' resolves as www.example.com.  Only the
          first domain is used.

     domain name
          A single search domain; equivalent to `search name'.

FILES
     /etc/resolv.conf

SEE ALSO
     host(1), gethostbyname(3), hosts(5), dhclient(8)

BUGS
     Only one nameserver and one search domain are honored; BSD's
     multiple-server failover and full search list are not
     implemented.



